R2 requirement:
- A call through an injected service or an interface links to the declaration that the type checker establishes. It also links to every implementation the type checker's implementation lookup finds.
- An implementation in a test file is labelled a test fake, with its file, and does not make the target ambiguous.
- When the lookup finds no implementation outside test files, the tool marks the target unresolved; when it finds more than one, it marks the target ambiguous and lists them all.
- Fails if:
  - an implementation the lookup finds has no link;
  - a declaration is presented as proof of an implementation;
  - a test fake is unlabelled or presented as the real implementation;
  - an unresolved or ambiguous target is unmarked.

